msgid "Choose a plan"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:219
msgid "Plan Details"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:224
msgid "The details, before you ask"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:272
#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:277
#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:282
msgid "Before you write"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:273
msgid "How quickly will I hear back?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:274
msgid "One working day for almost everything. If it is going to take longer than that, you get a message saying so rather than silence."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:278
msgid "What should I include?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:279
msgid "The page it happens on, what you expected, and what happened instead. A screenshot saves a whole exchange."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:283
msgid "Can I attach a file?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:284
msgid "Not to this form. Send the question first and reply to the email that comes back with anything you need to attach."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:287
#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:292
msgid "After you write"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:288
msgid "Will my question end up on this page?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:289
msgid "Possibly, if it is one other people will have too — reworded, and never with your name or email on it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:293
msgid "Who reads it?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:294
msgid "The support team, and every one gets read. There is no queue you can be dropped from without a reply."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:301
msgid "Ask us directly"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:302
msgid "One working day, and a person on the other end."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:334
msgid "Ask While You Read"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:339
msgid "Cannot find it? Ask."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:340
msgid "The form is on the left. The answers most people were looking for are on the right."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:366
msgid "Use the forgotten-password link on the sign-in page. The email arrives within a minute and the link is good for an hour."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:370
msgid "Can I change the email on my account?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:371
msgid "Yes, from Account settings. You will need to confirm it from the new address before it takes effect."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:375
msgid "How do I add someone to my team?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:376
msgid "Invite them by email from the Team page. They get their own sign-in and you decide what they can change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:380
msgid "Where is my licence key?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:381
msgid "On the order confirmation and in your account under Purchases. It never expires, even if the licence lapses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:385
msgid "Can I get a VAT invoice?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:386
msgid "Every order produces one automatically. Add your company details before paying and they will be on it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:390
msgid "Which PHP versions are supported?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:391
msgid "7.4 and above, and we test on the two most recent. Anything older will run but stops getting security fixes from us."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:395
msgid "Still stuck?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:396
msgid "Search is faster than we are, but if it is not in there we would rather hear from you than have you give up."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:399
msgid "Replies within one working day"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:400
msgid "Monday to Friday, 09:00 to 17:00 UTC"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:401
msgid "Answered by the people who built it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:404
msgid "Contact support"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:407
msgid "Search Then Ask"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:433
msgid "From the WordPress dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:434
msgid "Plugins, Add New, search for it, Install, Activate. Nothing appears on your pages until you place a block."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:438
msgid "By uploading the zip"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:439
msgid "Plugins, Add New, Upload Plugin. If an older copy is already there, deactivate it first — your questions are kept either way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:446
msgid "Placing your first block"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:447
msgid "Open a page, add the FAQ block, type a question. The answer box appears underneath and can be left for later."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:451
msgid "Reusing questions across pages"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:452
msgid "Save the block as a synced pattern, then place it. One edit updates every page carrying it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:456
msgid "Using it inside a page builder"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:457
msgid "Copy the shortcode from the group and paste it into any text widget the builder gives you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:463
msgid "Installing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:464
msgid "Two ways in, both about a minute."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:470
msgid "Your first FAQ"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:471
msgid "From an empty page to something published."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:476
msgid "Search engines and schema"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:477
msgid "Keep FAQ markup on one block per page. More than one set competes with itself and neither is reliably read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:481
msgid "Getting help"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:482
msgid "The form on the support page reaches the people who wrote this. Include the page and what you expected to happen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:487
msgid "Each heading opens into the specific cases underneath it, so you can stay at the top level until something matches."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:490
msgid "Start at the top and work down"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:491
msgid "One branch open at a time, so nothing scrolls away"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:492
msgid "Everything here also works from search"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:495
msgid "Full documentation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:498
msgid "Documentation Tree"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:503
msgid "Documentation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:547
#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:552
msgid "Layouts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:548
msgid "Can I use more than one layout on a page?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:549
msgid "Yes, as many as you like. Keep FAQ schema switched on for only one of them so the markup stays valid."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:553
msgid "Do the layouts share their questions?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:554
msgid "If you point them at the same group, yes. Editing the group updates every block showing it, in whatever layout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:557
#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:562
msgid "Styling"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:558
#: includes/Templates/ShowcaseSet.php:815
msgid "How much can I change?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:559
msgid "Colours, type, spacing, borders and behaviour, per block. It inherits your theme first, so it looks right before you touch anything."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:563
msgid "Will an update overwrite my styling?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:564
msgid "No. Everything you set is stored with the block in your post content, not in the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:568
msgid "Can questions come from my posts?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:569
msgid "Post FAQ turns any post type into an FAQ list, using the title as the question and the excerpt as the answer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:573
msgid "What happens to questions visitors send?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:574
msgid "They arrive under Form Submissions, where you can read each one, reply by email and mark it answered once it is handled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:578
msgid "Built to be lived in"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:579
msgid "The parts that matter after the first week: one library behind every block, styling that survives updates, and somewhere for the questions you did not think of."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:582
msgid "One library, every layout"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:583
msgid "Per-block styling, stored with your content"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:584
msgid "Submissions become answers in a click"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:585
msgid "Schema handled, on the block you choose"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:588
msgid "See every feature"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:601
msgid "Feature Tour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:606
msgid "What it does, in detail"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:629
msgid "Knowledge Hub"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:634
msgid "Find it, or just ask"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:635
msgid "Browse what we have written, or type the question and let it find the answer for you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:640
msgid "Recent articles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:658
msgid "More articles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:676
msgid "What do you need to know?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:677
msgid "Answered from the articles beside this, with links to the ones it used."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:681
msgid "Still need a person?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:686
msgid "How do I reuse questions across pages?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:687
msgid "Which layout is best for a pricing page?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:688
msgid "How do I add FAQ schema?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:714
msgid "Where do I begin?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:715
msgid "Add one block to one page and write one question. Everything else in here is something you can come back for."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:719
msgid "Do I need to configure anything first?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:720
msgid "No. There is no settings page you have to visit before the first block works."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:723
#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:728
msgid "Using it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:724
msgid "How do I change how it looks?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:725
msgid "Select the block and use the Style tab. Themes change the whole layout; the controls under them change one thing at a time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:729
msgid "Can two pages share the same questions?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:730
msgid "Save them as a group and place the group on both. One edit reaches every page carrying it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:734
msgid "Nothing shows on the page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:735
msgid "Clear the cache and hard refresh first — that is nine times in ten. After that, check the block is not filtered to an empty category."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:739
msgid "The AI answer was wrong"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:740
msgid "Mark it unhelpful and it is logged with the question. It answers from your own FAQs, so a wrong answer usually means one of them needs rewording."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:745
msgid "AI Answer Desk"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:750
msgid "Ask, and read on"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:751
msgid "Type the question. If the answer is already written, this finds it and says where it came from."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:756
#: build/blocks/ask-ai/index.js:356
msgid "Ask us anything"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:757
msgid "An instant answer from our own FAQs, with the sources it used."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:769
msgid "Can I use it on client sites?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/ProSet.php:770
msgid "What is the refund policy?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:56
msgid "Which size am I?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:57
msgid "Measure your chest and waist and read them off the chart, rather than going by the size you usually take. Ours run a little generous through the shoulder."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:59
#: includes/Templates/ShowcaseSet.php:799
msgid "Start here"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:63
msgid "Between two sizes?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:64
msgid "Take the smaller one in knitwear and the larger in outerwear. Knits relax with wear; a coat has to close over a jumper."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:69
msgid "Will it shrink?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:70
msgid "Everything is pre-washed, so no more than a percent or so. Wash cool and dry flat and it will hold its shape."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:75
msgid "What if it does not fit?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:76
msgid "Send it back within thirty days, unworn, and we pay the postage. Exchanges for a different size ship the same day we receive it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:81
msgid "Do you alter?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:82
msgid "Trousers and jackets, free, in any of our shops. Allow three working days, or a week in December."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:87
msgid "Are the sizes UK or EU?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:88
msgid "UK on the label, with EU and US on the chart. If you are ordering from outside the UK, go by the measurements."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:94
msgid "Size & Fit Guide"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:99
msgid "Size and fit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:100
msgid "The six things people ask before ordering. All of it on the page — no clicking."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:130
msgid "Do I need a visa?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:131
msgid "It depends on your passport, not on us. We send the requirement for your nationality with the booking confirmation, and again a month before you fly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:133
msgid "Check first"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:137
msgid "Any vaccinations?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:138
msgid "None are compulsory on any of our trips. Two are recommended for the desert itinerary — ask your GP eight weeks ahead, not two."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:143
msgid "Cash or card?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:144
msgid "Cards work in the cities and nowhere else on three of the four trips. Bring enough cash for a week and top up when you can."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:149
msgid "How much can I bring?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:150
msgid "One bag of twenty kilos and a daypack. On the walking trips a porter carries the large bag, so weight matters more than size."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:155
msgid "What is the weather like?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:156
msgid "Each itinerary lists the average high, low and rainfall by month. We only run trips in the months that read well."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:161
msgid "Is insurance included?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:162
msgid "No, and you cannot travel with us without it. Medical cover and repatriation are the two parts we check."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:168
msgid "Before You Travel"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:173
msgid "Before you travel"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:174
msgid "The paperwork and the packing, in the order people worry about them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:207
msgid "Which dishes contain nuts?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:208
msgid "Three on the current menu, all marked. The kitchen is not nut free, so we will not tell you that traces are impossible — we will tell you exactly which surfaces and pans are shared."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:212
msgid "Can a dish be made without them?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:213
msgid "Two of the three, yes, and it is cooked separately. The third is built on a nut base and we would rather say no than serve you something risky."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:220
msgid "What is gluten free as it comes?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:221
msgid "Eleven dishes, marked on the menu. The bread and two of the puddings are the only things that cannot be adapted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:225
msgid "Is it coeliac safe?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:226
msgid "We use a separate fryer and separate boards, and flour is handled at the other end of the kitchen. Tell your server it is coeliac rather than a preference and the ticket is flagged."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:233
msgid "How many dishes are vegan?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:234
msgid "Nine, and six of them are on the menu because they are good rather than because they are vegan. The small plates section is almost entirely plant based."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:238
msgid "Is the wine list vegan?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:239
msgid "Most of it. The list marks the four that are not, all of them fined with egg white."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:245
msgid "Nuts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:246
msgid "The kitchen is not nut free. Here is exactly where they appear."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:252
msgid "Gluten"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:253
msgid "What is safe as it comes, and what we can adapt."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:258
msgid "Vegan and vegetarian"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:259
msgid "Nine vegan dishes, and an honest note about the wine."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:264
msgid "Something else"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:265
msgid "Ring us before you book rather than asking on the night. The kitchen can plan around almost anything with a day's notice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:272
msgid "A colourful vegetable and chickpea bowl"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:284
msgid "Allergens & Dietary"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:325
msgid "How many sessions will I need?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:326
msgid "Four to six for most people, spread over a couple of months. You should feel a difference by the second — if you do not, we will say so and refer you on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:330
msgid "Do I need a scan first?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:331
msgid "Usually not. Imaging changes the plan in fewer than one case in ten, and an unnecessary scan tends to find something harmless that then worries you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:338
msgid "Is it worth it if I am older?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:339
msgid "Age is not the deciding factor — how much you move already is. Our oldest patient last year was eighty-four and finished the programme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:343
msgid "Will I need surgery eventually?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:344
msgid "Sometimes, and we will tell you when we think so rather than selling you sessions first. Getting stronger beforehand improves the outcome either way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:351
msgid "How soon can I train again?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:352
msgid "Something on the first day, almost always — modified, not nothing. Complete rest is the slowest way back for most injuries."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:356
msgid "Do you work with my coach?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:357
msgid "Gladly, with your permission. The programmes that hold are the ones where the coach knows what we have asked for."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:363
msgid "Back and neck"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:364
msgid "The most common reason people come to us, and the one with the most myths attached."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:370
msgid "Joints and arthritis"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:371
msgid "What is realistic, and when we would send you elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:376
msgid "Sports injuries"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:377
msgid "Getting back to it, sooner than resting would allow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:382
msgid "Not sure which applies"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:383
msgid "Book a fifteen-minute call. It is free, it is with a clinician rather than a receptionist, and it often ends with us telling you that you do not need us."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:395
msgid "A stethoscope beside a laptop at a clinic desk"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:407
msgid "Treatment Explorer"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:448
msgid "How often, and for how long?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:449
msgid "Three sessions a week for twelve weeks, forty-five minutes each. Missing one is fine; missing a fortnight means starting the block again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:453
msgid "Do I need a gym?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:454
msgid "From week five, yes, or a barbell at home. The first four weeks need a floor and a pair of bands."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:461
msgid "How fast will I lose weight?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:462
msgid "Half a kilo a week is the honest answer and the one that lasts. Anything faster is mostly water and comes back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:466
msgid "Do I have to count calories?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:467
msgid "Only if it suits you. Most people do better on portion habits and stop tracking within a month either way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:474
msgid "I have never run before"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:475
msgid "Then start on the walk-run weeks rather than skipping them. Everyone who gets injured in the first month skipped them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:479
msgid "Can I train for a specific race?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:480
msgid "Yes — give us the date and the distance and the block is built backwards from it, with a taper that actually tapers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:486
msgid "I want to get stronger"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:487
msgid "Twelve weeks, three sessions a week, measurable at the end."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:493
msgid "I want to lose weight"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:494
msgid "Slower than the internet promises, and it stays off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:499
msgid "I want to run further"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:500
msgid "From nothing to a distance, or from a distance to a faster one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:505
msgid "I do not know yet"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:506
msgid "Come in for an assessment. It costs nothing, takes half an hour, and ends with a recommendation you can take elsewhere if you want to."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:511
msgid "Programme Explorer"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:516
msgid "What are you training for?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:517
msgid "Pick the goal and the programme underneath it explains itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:553
msgid "Fixed price or day rate?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:554
msgid "Fixed, wherever the work can be described. Day rate only for open-ended discovery, and we will tell you which one applies before you ask."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:558
msgid "What is the smallest project you take?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:559
msgid "About a week. Below that the writing-it-down costs more than the work, and you are better off with someone hourly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:563
msgid "When do we pay?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:564
msgid "A third to start, a third at the halfway review, a third on handover. No invoice arrives before the thing it covers exists."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:571
msgid "What counts as a change?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:572
msgid "Anything that moves the date or the price. Reworded copy and a different shade of blue do not; a new page does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:576
msgid "How is it agreed?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Templates/SectorSet.php:577
